Deadline has partnered with The Brit List to profile some of the emerging writers who have made this year's ranking of the best unproduced UK film and TV projects. Launched in 2007, The Brit List has previously featured projects including The King's Speech and Responsible Child. Here, we profile Archie Thomson , who has made the list with Petroc.

Archie Thomson, the British writer who got his breakthrough on James McAvoy feature California Schemin &#8216; , was raised in West Country England, studied history at university, and has a &#8220;healthy taste for the epic.&#8221; So it's little wonder then that he made The Brit List this year with a TV series script about a Cornish crime saga, infused with local folklore and inspired by the work of Taylor Sheridan. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dsk-tab-mid-article1-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid","mid-articleX","mid-article","300x251"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[2,2],[300,250],[620,350],[300,251],[501,282],[3,3],[2,4],[4,2],[620,366]]) .exemptFromSleep() .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; }); Related Stories News Brit List 2026: Crime Series & Coming-Of-Age Movie Lead List Of Best Unproduced Screenplays News James McAvoy's Feature Directorial Debut 'California Schemin'' Sets Fall Release Via Magenta Light Studios

Petroc spotlights a charismatic and volatile Cornish outlaw who returns home after 12 years in prison. He sets about reclaiming what he believes has been taken from his family, transforming the Penroses from small-time crooks into a rising criminal power. Thomson jokes that Petroc is closer to Sicario than Poldark , the sweeping BBC drama that has become synonymous with Cornwall's depiction on screen. Watch on Deadline if ( !window.pmc.harmony?.isEventAdScheduledTime() ) { pmcCnx.cmd.push(function() { pmcCnx({ settings: { plugins: { pmcAtlasMG: { iabPlcmt: 2, } } }, playerId: '32fe25c4-79aa-406a-af44-69b41e969e71', playlistId: '0199e506-e642-7728-8264-463efe71337b', }).render("connatix_contextual_player_div"); }); } else { // This should only be get called when page cache is not cleared and it's event time. window.pmc.harmony?.switchToHarmonyPlayer(); }

&#8220;Taylor Sheridan's got a three-film run: Sicario , Wind River , and Hell or High Water . They're spare neo-Western crime dramas that really encapsulate the left-behind Rust Belt feeling of that part of America and the scale of the landscape. I remember thinking, why not do that? Why not draw on those mythic archetypes from Westerns and put them into an unfamiliar, striking setting like Cornwall?&#8221;

Petroc is set inland, rather than along Cornwall's fudge-box coastline, and gestures at the faded tin mining industry and local history. &#8220;Cornwall [on screen] is all Poldark and fancy houses and shots of waves crashing against the beach, whereas I wanted to get something a bit rawer, more rugged and truer to inland Cornwall,&#8221; Thomson explains.

The series is in with About Premium Content ( Keeping Faith ) and Cornwall's Bosena ( Rose of Nevada ). Thomson says the producers are just going to market with the script, which was ranked in the top three unhoused projects by The Brit List. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dl-mid-article-inject2-uid1' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article2","mid-articleX","mid-article","mid","300x251"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article2") .addSize([[300,250],[300,251],[620,350],[2,4],[4,2],[620,366]]) .exemptFromSleep() .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

Thomson first turned his hand to writing scripts during university, where his obsession with Game of Thrones fuelled a desire to write a TV series about the Norman conquest of England. His spec script helped open doors to writers' rooms, including alongside Dustin Lance Black on Under the Banner of Heaven .

Thomson took on a low-paid gig adapting Gavin Bain's 2010 book California Schemin' into a feature film, which, to his amazement, ended up in the hands of McAvoy. Set in the 1990s, it follows Bain and Billy Boyd, aspiring musicians whose ambitions were dismissed because of their Scottish accents. They reinvent themselves as California rappers, re-recording their tracks with American accents and arriving in London with a fabricated backstory that included ties to Eminem. Their gamble pays off: A record deal, sizable advances, and even an appearance on MTV.

McAvoy directed and starred in the movie, which had a U.S. release last month through Bob Yari's Magenta Light Studios . It was the first time Thomson saw actors voicing his words. &#8220;It's a music biopic, of course, so there's this big stage scene. It was filmed at the Barrowlands in Glasgow, and hundreds and hundreds of people turned up as free extras. I was watching them rap on stage. I was like: This is wild. I was in my bedroom writing this scene, and there it is.&#8221;

Thomson is spinning other plates, including an adaptation of Joseph Conrad's The Secret Agent , which came about after he scoured books that were out of copyright. The BBC adapted The Secret Agent in 2016 with Stephen Graham and Toby Jones, but Thomson is dragging the novel into the 21st century with a One Battle After Another twist. He's working with Submarine on the series.

&#8220;We've updated it and made it about concerns around AI encroachment into British security establishments, and people who are deeply opposed to tech and data centres. It's satirising that entire conversation and making it funny and dark,&#8221; he explains.

Other projects include an adaptation of Hungarian film Kills on Wheels , about two disabled teenagers who become assassins, and an original film titled Under The Black Mountain , a Zodiac -style thriller about satanic panic in 1970s Belfast.

Thomson is not short of ambition. &#8220;I suppose I'm quite interested in cinematic TV, if that makes sense. The stuff that can feel quite hard to get away with at the moment, in terms of being authored and premium,&#8221; he says. &#8220;I would love to have my own show and for it to be with HBO.&#8221;

On October 14, 2005, Daniel Craig was announced as the next James Bond via speedboat.

Yes, really &#x2014;&#xA0;the 007 actor was escorted by a convoy of Royal Marine Rigid Raider Speedboats to a press conference on London's River Thames, where a horde of journalists mostly asked him about his blond hair and rumored relationship with Sienna Miller.

Amazon MGM Studios &#8216; Robert Pattinson announcement couldn't have been a further departure from that grand entrance on Monday. Emerging from the shadows in a 25-second social media video was the 40-year-old: tuxedo on, eyes straight ahead, gun in hand. Simple, yet effective, it would seem &#x2014;&#xA0;the post has accrued over 1.2 million likes on X at the time of writing. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-article-mid-article-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid-articleX","mid","mid-article"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[300,250],[2,2],[300,251],[620,350],[2,4],[4,2],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450],[4,4],[300,251]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; }); Related Stories Business Niv Fichman's Rhombus Media Sells to Skywild Pictures (Exclusive) Business How Sky Studios Elstree Built for the Future

The new era for Bond has arrived. He's slick, sharp, and has undeniable rizz.

Cue the viral fancams of his Bond-ish Tenet character, Neil, soundtracked by the latest head-bopping Bond theme mix, and smash-hit X posts accusing the star of taking their job. &#8220;If you have a job right now, that's because Robert Pattinson didn't want it,&#8221; reads one post with over 180,000 likes.

No cap, Pattinson is on a storming run of form this year with The Drama , The Odyssey , Primetime and the upcoming Dune 3 . His casting announcement marks the first Bond in our frenzied pop cultural climate, where clicks are king and everyone's (often mid) opinion is immediately broadcast to the masses. It's only fitting that the reaction to his casting be as 2026 as possible. After all, Pattinson is Gen Z ( or so he says ). blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dsk-tab-mid-article2-uid1' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid","mid-article2","mid-articleX"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article2") .addSize([[300,250],[300,251],[620,350],[2,4],[4,2],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450],[4,4]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

His face was plastered across all major U.K. news sites, with the BBC and Sky News among those kicking off a live blog thread to round up the incoming reaction. Online, the actor was immediately accused of possessing &#8220;the greed they talk about in the bible&#8221; by nabbing both DC superhero Batman and Ian Fleming's iconic MI6 agent.

And after mogging the likes of Jack Lowden, Josh O'Connor, Callum Turner and Nicholas Hoult in the final Bond screen tests, he was also mogging the British public in London's famed Piccadilly Circus. On Monday, the paymasters at Amazon found the necessary number of pounds sterling to see Pattinson's chiseled cheekbones ascend to a lofty digital perch in a direct staredown with the Statue of Eros.

Having endured another annus horribilis of scandal and terrible PR, the royal family muscled in on the iconic moment by taking to X and glazing Pattinson. &#8220;Welcome to His Majesty's Secret Service, Mr Bond,&#8221; King Charles' team wrote. Even with their hall-of-fame London Olympic ceremony team-up in 2012, it's hard to imagine the late Elizabeth II making such a public declaration of faith early on in Craig's Bond tenure. The royals' post has been viewed 5.4 million times, an uptick of 5.3 million from King Charles' visit to the provincial English town of Preston on Monday. Fun fact: Pattinson will be the first-ever Bond to serve under a king. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-thr-article-mid-articleX-uid2' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["btf","mid-articleX","mid"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-articleX") .addSize([[300,250],[300,251],[620,350],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450],[4,4]]) .setLazyLoadMultiplier(2) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

It wasn't just the scandal-plagued royals trying to ride the Bond enthusiasm &#x2014;&#xA0;beleaguered Trump administration apparatchiks were also trying to get in on the fun. Always keen to ruin a good news story, Secretary of Health and Human Services Robert F. Kennedy Jr. used his official government X account to tweet out an AI-generated image of himself holding a carrot like a gun, a play on Pattinson's image. The frankenstein photo was captioned with the decidedly unfunny legend: &#8220;Food. Real Food.&#8221;

The Twilight stans are claiming to have played a small role in Pattinson's stratospheric rise to stardom, with many women on social media remarking on their early investment in his career. In all honesty, they ate with that: The vampiric and (by Pattinson's own admission) comically brooding Edward Cullen was adored by fans all over the world, but Pattinson was years away from solidifying his reputation as a once-in-a-generation talent and film bro fave through performances in the likes of Good Time , The Lighthouse and Die My Love . Look at him now.

In fact, Twilight might even have predicted Pattinson's Bond role: About halfway through Twilight , the first installment in the beloved film saga, Swan's high school friend group is seen discussing the theme for the upcoming prom, which is revealed to be Monte Carlo. &#8220;Gambling, tuxedos, and Bond, James Bond," Eric (Justin Chon) quips in the scene. A shocked Angela (Christian Serratos) then says, "Oh my God," as the camera cuts to a smirking Pattinson parking up as Edward. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-thr-article-mid-articleX-uid3' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["btf","mid-articleX","mid"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-articleX") .addSize([[300,250],[300,251],[620,350],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450],[4,4]]) .setLazyLoadMultiplier(2) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

While Google salutes the news by incorporating a funky graphic into search results for Pattinson's name &#x2014; his photos are shaken, not stirred, and served with a zest of lemon &#x2014;&#xA0;a host of soccer-related X accounts clawed their way into the news by making sure everyone knew that Pattinson was an Arsenal fan. It has often been said online that Pattinson is on a generational run in 2026 professionally, but let's not forget his soccer team won its first Premier League title this year since 2004. Like his fellow Gooners (that's an Arsenal fan, for those of you smirking), New York's Mayor Zohran Mamdani, Odyssey director Christopher Nolan and co-star Anne Hathaway, Pattinson is winning big time in life and on the field right now.

Sue Sylvester may soon be terrorizing the students of William McKinley High School once again &#x2014; that is, if Jane Lynch has anything to do with it.

After the &#8220; Glee &#8221; reboot was officially greenlit last month at Disney+ and Hulu, speculation started swirling about who from the original cast might return. During an appearance on &#8220;The Jennifer Hudson Show&#8221; on Monday, Lynch made it clear that she'd be happy to reprise her role as the foul-mouthed cheer coach. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-variety-article-mid-article-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid-articleX","mid","mid-article"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[300,250],[2,2],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; }); Related Stories Netflix’s 'Haunted Hotel' Renewed for Season 3 Netflix Launches First AI-Branded Content Recommendations Feature on TVs

&#8220;If I am asked to partake, the answer will be yes,&#8221; Lynch told Hudson. &#8220;I cannot wait.&#8221;

Asked what it would be like to revisit the character, Lynch said: &#8220;Oh, I would love to do Sue Sylvester for the rest of my life. You know, I wonder though how far we can take her now. Because if you look out in the world, there are a lot of Sue Sylvesters out there.&#8221;

Indeed, the Emmy winner previously said in a 2022 interview with The Guardian that Sylvester &#8220;would be MAGA&#8221; if &#8220;Glee&#8221; ever came back. She added that if the show were airing today, "I think there would have been people out there who would have wanted to cancel Sue Sylvester.&#8221;

However, she told Hudson that &#8220;it would be really, really fun to do it again and to get to wear tracksuits every day. That was my most favorite wardrobe.&#8221;

As for the rest of the original cast, Variety has confirmed that Lea Michele will be returning as Glee Club leader Rachel Berry. Several other original stars have also expressed their interest in taking part in the reboot, including Kurt Hummel actor Chris Colfer , who told The Daily Beast's &#8220;Obsessed&#8221; podcast last week that conversations about his return are ongoing. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dsk-tab-mid-article2-uid1' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid","mid-article2","mid-articleX"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article2") .addSize([[320,480],[300,250],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

"From what I heard, it sounded very funny and it sounded like a good idea. So we'll see,&#8221; Colfer said, even pitching some potential Kurt storylines: "I would love to see him like a Miranda Priestly-type, running his own fashion blog or a magazine. I could also see him on tour with Chappell Roan, styling her. There's a lot of fun avenues they could explore."

Watch Lynch's full interview with Hudson below.

The Walt Disney Co. smashed Wall Street expectations in its latest quarter, its fiscal Q4, with all three of its core divisions: Entertainment, experiences and sports, posting double digit year over year growth despite what the company described as a &#8220;challenging macroeconomic environment.&#8221;

Revenues rose 16% to $25.9 billion in the quarter with segment operating income soaring by 43% to $5 billion, and adjusted earnings per share rising to $1.77. The company told the street that it expects to continue seeing double digit EPS growth in fiscal 2027. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-article-mid-article-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid-articleX","mid","mid-article"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[300,250],[2,2],[300,251],[620,350],[2,4],[4,2],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450],[4,4],[300,251]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; }); Related Stories TV Brenda Song Says She Felt "Underpaid and Overworked" on Disney's 'The Suite Life' Shows TV 'Frozen' Is Getting the 'A Real Bug's Life' Treatment With Nat Geo, Disney+ and Hulu's 'The Real Frozen'

In the quarterly shareholder letter, CEO Josh D'Amaro and CEO Hugh Johnston once again outlined the moves the company is making around their three core pillars of investing in IP and creativity; Using technology to power storytelling and increase returns; and the One Disney model that they are implementing.

&#8220;Creativity and the pursuit of creative excellence will always be at the core of our company,&#8221; they wrote. &#8220;The increased engagement we saw across our streaming platforms and networks in the fourth quarter, which directly supports our revenue growth, reflects the strength of our creative talent, our focused investment in storytelling, and our leading sports rights portfolio.&#8221;

Disney's entertainment division saw revenues of $11.9 billion and operating income of $1.3 billion, thanks to continues growth in streaming at Disney+ and Hulu, and due to the theatrical performance of Spider Man: Brand New Day .

Experiences had revenues of $10.1 billion and operating income of $2.25 billion as per capita spending, increased domestic parks attendance and growth internationally helped offset a decrease in international visitors. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dsk-tab-mid-article2-uid1' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid","mid-article2","mid-articleX"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article2") .addSize([[300,250],[300,251],[620,350],[2,4],[4,2],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450],[4,4]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

Sports had revenue of $4.6 billion and operating income of $1.4 billion, with the company touting strong football viewership and ESPN's contributions to the overall streaming ecosystem.

But the company also disclosed a plan to change how it reports earnings to Wall Street, and while some of the changes are logical (consumer products will now be part of the entertainment division, A+E was sold to Hearst), the company will also end standalone disclosure of streaming operating income, which, combined with the move to pare back subscriber numbers, will mean less granular data around the sector.

&#8220;We have made strong progress scaling our SVOD businesses and, as a result, see a long runway for growth and margin expansion at Disney Entertainment,&#8221; the executives write in the letter. &#8220;We no longer believe the supplemental disclosure of SVOD operating income reflects this segment focus and strategy. Accordingly, we do not plan to continue providing this disclosure going forward.&#8221;

SVOD revenue was $6.1 billion in the quarter, with operating income of $824 million.

The letter also addressed the layoffs that have flowed through the company over the course of the year, with the executives writing that the company will &#8220;realize annual run-rate operating expense savings of approximately $3 billion by fiscal 2029. While these efficiencies will be used primarily to fund future growth, we do expect a portion to drop to the bottom line over time.&#8221;

In fiscal 2027, Disney projects double digit EPS growth, segment operating income growth of about 8%, and capex of $9 billion thanks to its long-term experiences investment.

The BBC and Canada's CBC have confirmed their adaptation of E.M. Forster's A Passage to India , casting Ali Fazal , Fiona Shaw and Tom Mison as leads.

The beloved book just turned 100. Set against the backdrop of the British Raj and directed by Emmy-winner Richie Mehta ( Delhi Crime) , the series will chart Aziz's optimistic attempts to prove to his Indian friends that cross-cultural friendship is possible under British rule, inspiring people to try and forge meaningful connections.

Aziz is being played by Fazal, an Indian star who has appeared in the likes of Victoria & Abdul and Mirzapur . Killing Eve star is Mrs. Moore, visiting her son Ronny (Gwilym Lee) in India, while Mison ( See) is Fielding, an elusive educator who grows close to Aziz. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dsk-tab-mid-article1-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid","mid-articleX","mid-article","300x251"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[2,2],[300,250],[620,350],[300,251],[501,282],[3,3],[2,4],[4,2],[620,366]]) .exemptFromSleep() .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; }); Related Stories News 'Doctor Who': BBC Draws Up Producer Shortlist As Race To Regenerate Iconic Series Moves To Next Stage News BBC Boss Confronted By Angry Staff Over "Banning" Of Trans Rights Symbols In TV Shows

The series is one of the most high-profile BBC adaptations in a while and counts Canada's CBC as co-producer. Nisha Parti's Parti Productions is making A Passage to India with Working Title and Mehta's indie A Passage Post. Watch on Deadline if ( !window.pmc.harmony?.isEventAdScheduledTime() ) { pmcCnx.cmd.push(function() { pmcCnx({ settings: { plugins: { pmcAtlasMG: { iabPlcmt: 2, } } }, playerId: '32fe25c4-79aa-406a-af44-69b41e969e71', playlistId: '0199e506-e642-7728-8264-463efe71337b', }).render("connatix_contextual_player_div"); }); } else { // This should only be get called when page cache is not cleared and it's event time. window.pmc.harmony?.switchToHarmonyPlayer(); }

Other cast includes Naseeruddin Shah ( Paar, The League of Extraordinary Gentlemen ) as Godbole, a fellow educator at Fielding's college and spiritual anchor in the face of the events unfolding around him. Shahana Goswami ( Santosh, Four Years Later ) is Amrit Rao, Aziz's elegant, intellectual and sophisticated barrister, who has recently qualified as India's first woman lawyer. Danish Hussain ( Haq, Tanaav ) is Hamidullah, Aziz's uncle and best friend.

The show was first revealed by Working Title exec Surian Fletcher-Jones who said at the time it would &#8220;reclaim colonial history" and &#8220;turn the novel on its head.&#8221;

Mehta said: &#8220;Adapting A Passage to India has been a dream of mine for as long as I've been telling stories. To reinterpret the complex and intriguing characters that E.M. Forster masterfully conjured from his experiences over a century ago, and finding in them a relevance that resonates so deeply with today's world, has been a real joy.&#8221;

Parti added: &#8220;After almost ten years of work alongside Richie, it's an honour to be bringing this epic story to television for the first time. To tell the story of British colonial rule, which shaped all our families, from an Indian perspective feels like a first. This beautiful novel tackles that and so much more. We've seen many romanticised versions of India on screen over the years, so I'm so grateful to Working Title Television and Universal Global Television for understanding why our version needs to be told now and helping bring it to life, and to the BBC and CBC for being such brilliant partners.&#8221;

Ali Fazal (&#8220;Mirzapur&#8221;), Tom Mison and Fiona Shaw are leading the cast of &#8220; A Passage to India ,&#8221; Emmy-winning &#8220;Delhi Crime&#8221; filmmaker Richie Mehta's five-part series version of E.M. Forster's classic novel for the BBC and the Canadian Broadcasting Corporation.

Mehta wrote the adaptation and is now directing it on location in India.

Set in the 1920s, the drama follows Aziz (Fazal), a local doctor who has spent years caring for others and who sets out to convince his Indian friends that real friendship with the British can survive colonial rule. His hopes start to come apart after an unexplained episode at the Marabar caves, which leaves him accused of assault. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-variety-article-mid-article-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid-articleX","mid","mid-article"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[300,250],[2,2],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; }); Related Stories Taiwan’s Chunghwa Telecom Unveils 10 Content Investments, From 'Gunshot' to 'Call of Lobster' ‘Pokemon’ Anime Studio OLM Trains AI Coloring Tool on Just Three Frames in Japan Government-Backed Project

The scandal stirs up violent feeling and builds to a trial that grips the public. As the case plays out, the lives of everyone involved are upended, and Aziz and those closest to him begin to grasp how deeply colonization has shaped them.

Mison (&#8220;De Gaulle: Resistance,&#8221; &#8220;See&#8221;) plays Fielding, an elusive teacher who becomes close to Aziz. BAFTA winner Shaw (&#8220;Bad Sisters,&#8221; &#8220;Killing Eve&#8221;) is Mrs. Moore, a woman who has led a varied life and who comes to India to see her son Ronny (Gwilym Lee, &#8220;The Great,&#8221; &#8220;Bohemian Rhapsody&#8221;) and set up a match between him and Adela (Clare Hughes, &#8220;Ponies,&#8221; &#8220;Ten Pound Poms&#8221;).

Naseeruddin Shah (&#8220;Paar,&#8221; &#8220;The League of Extraordinary Gentlemen&#8221;) plays Godbole, who teaches alongside Fielding at his college and offers spiritual grounding as the crisis deepens. Shahana Goswami (&#8220;Santosh,&#8221; &#8220;Four Years Later&#8221;) is Amrit Rao, Aziz's barrister, who has just become India's first woman lawyer. Danish Hussain (&#8220;Haq,&#8221; &#8220;Tanaav&#8221;) plays Hamidullah, Aziz's uncle and closest friend, who doubts the cross-cultural bonds Aziz believes in. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dsk-tab-mid-article2-uid1' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid","mid-article2","mid-articleX"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article2") .addSize([[320,480],[300,250],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

&#8220;Adapting &#8216;A Passage to India' has been a dream of mine for as long as I've been telling stories,&#8221; Mehta said. &#8220;To reinterpret the complex and intriguing characters that E.M. Forster masterfully conjured from his experiences over a century ago, and finding in them a relevance that resonates so deeply with today's world, has been a real joy, and I believe it makes for incredibly gripping drama.&#8221;

Parti Productions (&#8220;The Boy with the Topknot&#8221;), Working Title Television (&#8220;Jo Nesb&#xF8;'s Detective Hole&#8221;) and Mehta's A Passage Post, a subsidiary of his Poor Man's Productions (&#8220;Poacher&#8221;), are producing the show. The BBC and CBC commissioned it for BBC One, BBC iPlayer, CBC TV and CBC Gem, and it qualifies as an official U.K.-Canada co-production. Working Title Television sits within Universal Studio Group's Universal Global Television division. NBCUniversal Global TV Distribution is handling worldwide sales.

Nisha Parti, founder of Parti Productions and an executive producer on the show, said she was honored to be bringing the story to television after almost 10 years of working with Mehta. &#8220;To tell the story of British colonial rule, which shaped all our families, from an Indian perspective feels like a first. This beautiful novel tackles that and so much more,&#8221; she said. &#8220;We've seen many romanticized versions of India on screen over the years, so I'm so grateful to Working Title Television and Universal Global Television for understanding why our version needs to be told now and helping bring it to life, and to the BBC and CBC for being such brilliant partners.&#8221;

Mehta and Parti serve as executive producers along with Working Title Television's Surian Fletcher-Jones, Eric Fellner and Tim Bevan, the BBC's Nawfal Faizullah, CBC's Nicola Makoway and Roma Khanna. Kristian Dench is series producer.

&#8220;&#8216;A Passage to India' is one of the great stories about friendship, and how quickly suspicion and power can tear it apart,&#8221; said Fletcher-Jones, who is head of drama at Working Title Television. &#8220;Richie has understood that from the very start, and his scripts handle it with real care and honesty.&#8221;

Lindsay Salt, director of BBC Drama, said Mehta's pitch had blown the broadcaster away. &#8220;He has crafted a version of extraordinary depth and sensitivity, and we're thrilled to be working with him and our partners at Parti Productions, Working Title Television, A Passage Post and CBC,&#8221; she said. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-variety-article-mid-articleX-uid2' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["btf","mid-articleX","mid"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-articleX") .addSize([[320,480],[300,250],[300,251],[620,366]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

