&#8220;She'd been growing things for the war effort and was holding the most enormous bunch of carrots you've ever seen,&#8221; said Addy. &#8220;They were bigger than she was, and she was smiling at the camera. For whatever reason, when I looked at the photo, I thought, &#8216;Wow, this is probably the best time of your life.' She got to be outside growing vegetables, with all the freedom, independence and recognition that came with it.&#8221;

Addy's attention was grabbed by the picture and she recalled the story of both her grandmothers, one of whom looked after evacuees during the war and the other was a Red Cross nurse in London. &#8220;They always spoke about the war, strange as it sounds, as some of the best times of their lives,&#8221; said Addy. &#8220;It's such a complicated feeling, and it's always intrigued me.&#8221;

Addy therefore reflected on how while men were out fighting, a huge number of women suddenly found themselves joining the workforce. Relinquishing this from 1945 was anything but easy. &#8220;Those closing months were an uneasy time for women,&#8221; said Addy. &#8220;On the one hand, they're deeply relieved that the war is ending; on the other, they're deeply anxious about their own futures.&#8221;

These thoughts helped crystalize Dig for Victory in Addy's mind. The movie is set in rural Wiltshire, UK, as an isolated girl, Edith, comes of age during the closing months of World War Two. When a violent incident interrupts a new friendship with an older woman, Edith uncovers a series of secrets that will shape a deadly future. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dl-mid-article-inject2-uid1' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article2","mid-articleX","mid-article","mid","300x251"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article2") .addSize([[300,250],[300,251],[620,350],[2,4],[4,2],[620,366]]) .exemptFromSleep() .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

