Addy already has ideal cast in mind. While assuming young protagonist Edith would be played by a rising star, Addy's dream for the older woman is the &#8220;charismatic&#8221; and &#8220;captivating&#8221; Indira Varma. For Edith's mother, she settles on Emily Blunt.

Addy thinks the tone she's trying to achieve would be perfect for actors like Varma and Blunt. She was inspired by movies like Florence Pugh-starrer The Wonder and Olivia Colman's Wicked Little Letters, the latter of which is &#8220;darkly comic&#8221; and has a &#8220;main character who felt a little unusual,&#8221; she said. &#8220;I wanted it to be tense and foreboding,&#8221; added Addy. &#8220;Even though the war is at arm's length, there are still planes flying overhead and a sense of threat. I wanted it to feel a little edgy, with twists and turns that keep you on your toes.&#8221;

